Adobe's X11 bitmap fonts, the BDF files Mill Fonts is converted from (Times and Courier, regular,
bold, and oblique or italic), kept here so the suitcase can be rebuilt without a download. They are
unchanged from the releases:

  font-adobe-75dpi-1.0.4.tar.xz   https://www.x.org/releases/individual/font/font-adobe-75dpi-1.0.4.tar.xz
    SHA-256 1281a62dbeded169e495cae1a5b487e1f336f2b4d971d92911c59c103999b911
    -> 75dpi/   (the 8 to 24 pixel files fonts.json names)
  font-adobe-100dpi-1.0.4.tar.xz  https://www.x.org/releases/individual/font/font-adobe-100dpi-1.0.4.tar.xz
    SHA-256 b67aff445e056328d53f9732d39884f55dd8d303fc25af3dbba33a8ba35a9ccf
    -> 100dpi/  (the 8 and 24 point files fonts.json names)

COPYING is the releases' own license (the same in both): Adobe Systems Incorporated and Digital
Equipment Corporation, which allows use, copying, modification, distribution, and sale with the
copyright notices and the permission notice in supporting documentation. The notice also goes into
Mill Fonts itself and its Read Me. Each BDF file carries it in its header as well.

python3 ../../build.py --download reads the releases instead of these files and checks their SHA-256.
